{
  "summary": "The UI implementation largely passes automated accessibility (axe) and Lighthouse checks, and the primary navigation flow works without crashes. However, several mandatory screens/components and states from DESIGN.md are missing or incomplete, and a few accessibility and design‑token usage gaps remain. Missing the History screen, LedgerStatusCard, VerifyExportDialog, and the full offline‑banner implementation prevents the user from completing the core “audit‑ledger” flow. Some screens (PolicyGateScreen) lack the required error/retry UI, and a handful of icon‑only buttons are missing explicit accessibility labels. These issues are medium‑high priority and must be addressed before the product can be considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptDetailScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The History screen is not present in the project (no HistoryScreen component or route). DESIGN.md requires a dedicated HistoryScreen with default, loading, and empty (fallback) states accessible via the History icon button on the receipt/mileage detail screens.",
      "fix": "Create `src/screens/HistoryScreen.tsx` (and add a route in `src/navigation/index.tsx`). Implement the three states: default list with `HistoryList`, an overlay `ActivityIndicator` for loading, and a centered fallback view with the copy \"No history found.\". Ensure the screen respects the 56 dp header height and 44 × 44 dp minimum touch targets. Wire the History icon button (`accessibilityLabel=\"History\"`) to navigate to this screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "SettingsScreen displays ledger verification status but the `LedgerStatusCard` component referenced in DESIGN.md does not exist in the codebase. Consequently the verification text and warning UI are missing.",
      "fix": "Add a new component `src/components/ui/LedgerStatusCard.tsx` that uses the Material‑3 `Card` primitive, pulls colors/text from `theme` (primary text for verified, error text for warning, icons accordingly) and accepts props `status`, `entryCount`, `message`. Use this component at the top of SettingsScreen, passing the appropriate status based on ledger verification result."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Verify Export flow is described in DESIGN.md but there is no `VerifyExportDialog` component and no UI for picking a CSV file, pasting a verification code, or showing result dialogs.",
      "fix": "Create `src/components/ui/VerifyExportDialog.tsx` (or place it inside SettingsScreen). It should render a `Dialog` with a \"Pick CSV file\" button (`accessibilityLabel=\"Pick CSV file\"`), a `TextInput` labelled \"PDF verification code\", and a `PrimaryButton` labeled \"Verify\" that is disabled until either input is present. Implement loading, success, and error states displaying the exact copy from the spec. Wire the dialog open state to the \"Verify an export\" button at the bottom of SettingsScreen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The error state (full‑screen error view with a Retry button) required by the spec is not implemented. The screen only shows the default acceptance view and loading spinner.",
      "fix": "Add an error UI branch to `PolicyScreen` that displays a centered error message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" and a `PrimaryButton` labelled \"Retry\". The Retry button should re‑attempt storing the acceptance and reset any error flag."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/OfflineBanner.tsx (new file)",
      "issue": "Design calls for a full‑screen offline banner on every screen, but no component or global implementation exists. Users currently receive no indication when the device is offline.",
      "fix": "Create a reusable `OfflineBanner` component that renders a top‑anchored view with the copy \"You are offline. Some actions require an internet connection.\" using `theme.colors.error` on a surface background. Include it at the top of the `Screen` component so it appears on all screens, and toggle visibility via NetInfo or expo-network listener."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Icon‑only FABs (e.g., the Add receipt FAB) lack explicit `accessibilityLabel` props, making them invisible to screen readers.",
      "fix": "Update all icon‑only `FAB`/`Button` components (FABAdd, MiniFAB, ScanButton, History icon button) to include an `accessibilityLabel` that matches the visual intent (e.g., \"Add receipt\", \"Scan receipt\", \"History\", \"Verify export\"). Ensure `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` is also set."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/*",
      "issue": "Several components use hard‑coded color literals (e.g., `backgroundColor: '#FFFFFF'`) and spacing values (e.g., `margin: 16`) instead of the design tokens from `theme` (`theme.colors.surface`, `theme.spacing`). This bypasses the token system and may cause inconsistent theming.",
      "fix": "Replace all literal colors and spacing with references to `theme.colors.*` and `theme.spacing` (or `spacing * n`). For example, use `backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface` and `marginHorizontal: theme.spacing * 2`. Run a lint rule or create a TypeScript utility to enforce token usage."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus-visible outlines are not applied on web for buttons and inputs; the design requires a 2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`.",
      "fix": "Add a custom style for web (using `Platform.OS === 'web'`) that applies `outline: 2px solid ${theme.colors.outline}` on `:focus-visible` for `Button`, `TextInput`, and list items. Verify the outline appears when navigating via keyboard."
    }
  ]
}

