{
  "summary": "The new ledger implementation adds cryptographic chaining and size limits, but several security gaps remain. Append‑only guarantees are still reliant on the Store, entry data size is unbounded, and audit logging for edits/deletions is missing. Backup handling now enforces a 10 MiB size limit, fixing the original unbounded‑size risk, but ledger size limits are not enforced on restore, allowing a crafted backup to bypass the MAX_LEDGER_ENTRIES check. Two deployment‑level library vulnerabilities (node‑forge and braces) are still present. A new high‑severity denial‑of‑service risk was introduced because addLedgerEntry throws when the ledger reaches its entry limit, and the exception is not caught, potentially crashing the app. The CSP meta tag for the web fallback remains missing.",
  "previous": [
    {
      "id": "ledger-append-only",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; ledger is still stored as a mutable encrypted array and append‑only guarantee relies solely on store integrity."
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-entry-size",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; there is still no explicit limit on the size of a ledger entry's data field."
    },
    {
      "id": "photo-uri-path-traversal",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Fixed by adding strict validation of photoUri in validateBackupStructure (rejects '..' and absolute paths)."
    },
    {
      "id": "export-verification-code-leak",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "low",
      "severity_change_reason": "Fixed by adding a verification line to exports and not exposing sensitive internal state beyond the required short code."
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-csp-web",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "low",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; the web build still lacks a Content‑Security‑Policy meta tag."
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-unbounded-growth",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "low",
      "severity_change_reason": "Fixed by introducing a hard‑coded MAX_LEDGER_ENTRIES limit."
    },
    {
      "id": "backup-unbounded-size",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Fixed by enforcing MAX_BACKUP_BYTES (10 MiB) before encryption and after decryption, preventing oversized backups."
    },
    {
      "id": "backup-unknown-fields",
      "status": "fixed",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "Fixed by whitelisting receipt and mileage fields in validateBackupStructure; unexpected fields now cause validation failure."
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-missing-mod-log",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; receipt edits and deletions are still not recorded in the ledger."
    },
    {
      "id": "ledger-missing-mod-log-mileage",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; mileage edits and deletions are still not recorded in the ledger."
    },
    {
      "id": "node-forge-vuln",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; vulnerable node‑forge 1.4.0 remains in the dependency tree."
    },
    {
      "id": "braces-vuln",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "high",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; vulnerable braces 3.0.3 remains in the dependency tree."
    },
    {
      "id": "backup-ledger-size-bypass",
      "status": "open",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_change_reason": "No change; restoreBackup writes the ledger directly without enforcing the MAX_LEDGER_ENTRIES limit, allowing a crafted backup to exceed the intended size."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
