{
  "summary": "Overall the UI closely follows the DESIGN.md specification – all primary screens (PolicyGate, Dashboard, Receipt/Mileage entry, History, Settings, Backup/Restore) are present, navigation via the fixed BottomTabBar works, and the flows exercised by the headless tests succeed. Lighthouse reports a high accessibility score (98) and there are no axe violations. However a few spec‑defined states and accessibility details are missing or implemented incorrectly, and a handful of design‑token usages are inconsistent. Those gaps are captured below.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing error state – the spec requires a full‑screen error view with a Retry button when acceptance cannot be stored, but the component only implements Loading and Default states.",
      "fix": "Add a third UI branch that renders a centered error message \"Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.\" and a PrimaryButton labelled \"Retry\" that re‑invokes the acceptance flow. Use the theme colors (error background, onError text) and ensure the button is focus‑visible and accessible."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/OfflineBanner.tsx (missing)",
      "issue": "The globally required offline banner (full‑screen banner at the top of every screen) is not present anywhere in the codebase.",
      "fix": "Create a new `OfflineBanner` component that uses the theme's surface color, displays the copy \"You are offline. Some actions require an internet connection.\", and is rendered conditionally at the top of the `Screen` component (or via a context provider). Ensure it has role=\"alert\" and a visible focus outline for keyboard users."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/HistoryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing fallback empty state – the spec defines a centered view with the text \"No history found.\" for the (unlikely) empty case, but the component only handles Default and Loading states.",
      "fix": "Add an `EmptyHistory` view that matches the design tokens (spacing‑unit 8, bodyLarge typography) and conditionally render it when the entry list length is zero."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/LedgerStatusCard.tsx (missing)",
      "issue": "LedgerStatusCard component is not present, and the warning variant in SettingsScreen uses a red background instead of the surface background defined in the spec.",
      "fix": "Implement `LedgerStatusCard` as a separate component that accepts `status` (\"verified\" | \"warning\") and renders with a surface background. For the warning state use the error color only for the icon and text, leaving the card background unchanged. Pull colors from `theme.colors` and typography from `theme.typography`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/IconButton.tsx (or any icon‑only button usage)",
      "issue": "Icon‑only buttons (History icon, Scan, Verify Export, FABs) lack an explicit `accessibilityLabel`, which reduces screen‑reader discoverability.",
      "fix": "Add an `accessibilityLabel` prop to each icon‑only button instance (e.g. \"History\", \"Scan receipt\", \"Verify export\"). Ensure the prop is passed to the underlying Paper `IconButton` so that it appears as `aria-label` on web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Visible focus style is not implemented for web – the spec requires a 2 dp outline on focus‑visible, but the component only changes elevation on hover.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style rule (or `onFocus` handler) that applies a `border: 2px solid var(--color-outline)` around the button. Use the theme's `outline` color and ensure the outline is removed on blur."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields do not set appropriate `autoComplete` attributes (e.g. `autocomplete=\"off\"` for amount, `autocomplete=\"date\"` for date), which is a best‑practice for form usability.",
      "fix": "Pass `autoComplete` props to the underlying Paper `TextInput` based on the field type (e.g. `autoComplete=\"off\"` for numeric amount, `autoComplete=\"bday\"` for date) and document the mapping."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Spacing values are hard‑coded (e.g. `marginTop: 24`) instead of using the design token `spacing` (8 dp grid).",
      "fix": "Replace numeric spacing with `theme.spacing * N` or the CSS custom property `--spacing-unit` to keep vertical rhythm consistent across the app."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button height is set to 40 dp, which is below the required minimum tap target of 44 × 44 dp (48 dp height for comfortable tap).",
      "fix": "Adjust the button style to have a minimum height of 48 dp (or at least 44 dp) while keeping the visual design. Update any style overrides that force a smaller height."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/HistoryList.tsx",
      "issue": "List items do not enforce the minimum 56 dp height defined in the spec; the current `Card` style uses `padding: 12` only.",
      "fix": "Add a style rule `minHeight: 56` to each list item container and ensure the touch area covers the full width."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Dialog.tsx",
      "issue": "Dialog does not trap focus on web – users can tab to elements behind the dialog.",
      "fix": "Wrap the dialog content with a focus‑trap library (e.g., `focus-trap-react`) or use the `Portal`'s built‑in focus management to keep focus inside while open."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Snackbar.tsx",
      "issue": "Snackbar messages are not announced via live region, so screen‑reader users may miss transient notifications.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"` and `role=\"status\"` to the Snackbar component so that its content is announced."
    }
  ]
}

